Package: hcbic
Title: How Much Data Does It Take to Test an Expert Causal Diagram?
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Cory", "Whitney", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "cory.whitney@uni-bonn.de",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4988-4583"))
Description: Tools to ask how well data can support or contradict an
    expert-elicited causal diagram (a directed acyclic graph) of a farm
    system. The package holds one expert diagram of agroforestry and
    livelihoods, simulates data from it, runs hill-climbing structure
    learning scored by the Bayesian information criterion (BIC), and reports
    how many observations are needed to recover the diagram and to detect
    each missing arc.
